          "type": "text",
          "text": "**V10 in 6 weeks from V3 isn't happening — that's roughly a decade of grade jumps compressed into 6 weeks. Nobody's tendons/CNS adapt that fast, even with perfect training.** Realistic 6-week ceiling: solid V5 sends, V6 on good beta/day. For the comp, that's actually fine — most gym comps score on volume+difficulty across a spread of problems, not one flash grade. Real goal: **maximize your tick list across V4–V7, sharpen power and comp-day execution.**\n\n6-week structure:\n- **Wk1-2 (Base/Strength):** pull strength, antagonist balance, hangboard base, moderate volume bouldering\n- **Wk3-4 (Power):** limit bouldering, campus/contact strength, lower volume higher intensity\n- **Wk5 (Power-Endurance + Comp Sim):** circuits, redpointing comp-style problems, simulate flash-attempts\n- **Wk6 (Taper):** cut volume ~50%, keep intensity, max 2 climbing days, rest before comp\n\nBuilding Week 1 now:"
        },
